    "result_text": "The build is green: **Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0** \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `timezone` on the `Owner` response, derived from the owner's locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`LocalityResolver.java`** \u2014 added the `REGION_TIMEZONE` table (NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane) and a `timezoneOfRegion(String region)` method that returns the IANA name, or `null` for an unknown/`UNKNOWN` region.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `timezone` that resolves the region the same way `locality` does (`regionOfCustomerCode`) and passes it through `timezoneOfRegion`, so timezone stays consistent with the reported locality.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `timezone` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field.\n\nThe change follows the existing derivation pattern: locality is read off the owner's `customerCode` region, and timezone is now looked up from that same region. The acceptance test (Sydney owner \u2192 `locality` NSW, `timezone` Australia/Sydney) passes.",
